                            1. Running the demo.
                            ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ



Right in order to run this demo you need LOTS of memory, well not really,
but make sure that you have about 600k free. Also make sure that unless you
REALLY need it, that you don't use a memory manager - this slows the demo
down, and is generally a bhaaaad idea. The demo features quite a few mods,
so a Soundblaster/Soundblaster-Pro/SB-16/Gravis Ultra Sound would be a good
idea. Though don't worry - there's a 'NoSound' option for weenies,
shit happens :-).

